bug_report:
Rotate of a packetset causes different types to binary operator error
As reported on the gm2 mailing list, it looks as if there is missing conversion, maybe:


$ cat testrotate.mod
MODULE testrotate ;  

IMPORT SYSTEM;

VAR
  v: PACKEDSET OF [0..31];
  i: INTEGER;
BEGIN
  i := 3;
  v := SYSTEM.ROTATE (v, i);
END testrotate.


$ gm2 -fiso testrotate.mod 
testrotate.mod: In function ‘_M2_testrotate_init’:
testrotate.mod:10:8: error: not expecting different types to binary operator
   10 |   v := SYSTEM.ROTATE (v, i);
      |        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
